**BLUF:** (G1, Minor) PR 2085's body says cell LOG "pins that no key and no hash reach a log on the refused mint and revoke". The cell (line 344, "RED LOG-<state>") checks only `KEY` and `hashOf(KEY)`, the WARMED key; a refused mint generates a fresh one. Gate 248 planted the minted key and hash into the refused mint's log line: the log then carried both and LOG-C and LOG-D stayed green on 3 runs (a hash-only plant too). The product is clean unplanted: a guard pointing the wrong way, not a leak. Fix shape: assert the mint's log text has no `sk_` plus 64 hex and no 64-hex hash; the plant must red it. (G5, Info) the comment at `services/security/src/index.ts` lines 510 to 513 says the refusal sits after the memory write "on purpose"; moving it before the write reds 0 of 38, because with the flag down `dbGetApiKey` hands the route the map's own object and the mint's catch deletes its copy anyway: pin it or reword. Measured on a stubbed store. Refs KS-2074.
