**C4: COMMENT on KS-2122 (G301-2162-2, Info).** **BLUF:** PR 2162 (merged as `aa4ddb096053`, not on Kintsugi) pins the answer-equality property but not the no-read property its cell title claims: cell N4 (`services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks2122-notification-doors-refuse-connector-principals.test.ts` line 133, "... it reads no store") is not red for the gate's mutant that moves the delete refusal after the lookup and before the 404; the answer is the same. Not a product defect; the title says more than the cell sees. Gate 301 (12 other mutants caught); nothing ran in this comment.
**C5: COMMENT on KS-2011 (G313-2185-1 + -2).** **BLUF:** PR 2185 (merged as `c480a84e7f53`, not on Kintsugi) expires the api-gateway's in-memory notification settings 24 hours after their last write. User-visible, measured by gate 313: `GET /api/settings/notifications` (`services/api-gateway/src/routes/admin.ts` lines 1596 to 1603) answers `certificationNotifications: true` and `verificationNotifications: true` when the store returns null, so in fallback mode (Redis unavailable) a user who switched a notification OFF reads it ON again 24 hours after the last write. The Redis branch has always done this (TTL from the write, a read does not renew it): the PR makes the degraded mode consistent, but its body says "the getters answer null" and not what the route returns. Whether a 24-hour opt-out reset is acceptable in Redis mode is pre-existing. The lifetime is a design choice the ticket does not make: one expression, `TTL.privacy * 1000` in `services/api-gateway/src/services/redis.ts`. Nothing ran in this comment.

